                <pb facs="0503" n="433" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg433"/>

                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <p rendition="#center">Citizen Juan José Baz, political chief of the capital of the
                    republic, to its inhabitants makes known:</p>
                <p>That from the publication of this order all inspectors and sub-inspectors that
                    were in office in May, 1863, shall serve as policemen now, and present
                    themselves at the deputation for orders. Those that have served the empire are
                    excluded from this regulation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JUAN J. BAZ.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 21, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
